      "skill": "brainstorming",
      "mode": "equivalent",
      "summary": "Compared solution boundaries and acceptance behavior for measurable, auditable context reduction while retaining the approved workflow gates.",
      "reason": "The Superpowers brainstorming skill was not discoverable as an invocable skill in this Codex session. The repository feature-requirements Skill and Prompt were read; equivalent structured option analysis was performed without claiming the unavailable skill was invoked.",
      "questions": [
        "Should the tool report a file list or the exact text delivered to the Agent? Selected exact rendered text because only it can substantiate context size and omissions.",
        "Should the budget count source files or the assembled prompt? Selected normalized final bundle text plus distinct selected groups, matching what the Agent receives.",
        "Where should conditional selection rules live? In the existing authoritative stage-input configuration, avoiding a competing trigger registry.",
        "What if TASK details are missing? Return explicit PENDING fields and source gaps; never infer paths or checks from task titles."
      ],
      "alternatives": [
        "Keep list-only output and estimate size; rejected because expanded content, provenance, and final budget would remain unverified.",
        "Always read the complete baseline; rejected because it preserves the current context bloat and does not respect trigger-based inputs."
      ],
      "decisions": [
        "Add deterministic fail-closed JSON rendering with provenance and measured budget while retaining list and audit modes.",
        "Generate optional TASK ID execution cards strictly from authoritative artifacts, listing unresolved fields instead of guessing."
      ],
